1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,604
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:30,655
<i>Can I ask you a favor?</i>
<i>I want to call you Mama.</i>

6
00:00:30,739 --> 00:00:33,533
[Helena] <i>But, of course. Baby girl.</i>

7
00:00:33,616 --> 00:00:35,410
[Anna] <i>Do you know someone</i>
<i>who wants to help Lily?</i>

8
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:37,537
<i>-Natalie.</i>
<i>-Are you serious, Jepoy?</i>

9
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:39,080
<i>You actually trust that woman?</i>

10
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:41,624
[Jepoy] <i>You're so convinced that someone</i>
<i>like Arnaldo can change.</i>

11
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:44,586
<i>But now that Natalie wants to</i>
<i>help us, you think it's wrong.</i>

12
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:46,755
<i>The arms shipment with Mr. Yi</i>
<i>will push through.</i>

13
00:00:46,838 --> 00:00:52,677
[Helena] <i>And this is how Helena Montoya</i>
<i>becomes Red Dragon.</i>

14
00:00:52,761 --> 00:00:55,805
[Mercedes] <i>If you don't show up</i>
<i>to the operation later,</i>

15
00:00:55,889 --> 00:01:00,643
<i>this bullet will lodge itself in the head</i>
<i>of your beloved Camia.</i>

16
00:01:02,145 --> 00:01:04,981
[Lily] <i>Red Dragon is making</i>
<i>a shipment tonight.</i>

17
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,400
[Diego] <i>I'll sabotage their delivery.</i>

18
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:11,029
[Lily] <i>Mom, I have to find a way</i>
<i>to help Diego's plan succeed.</i>

19
00:01:11,529 --> 00:01:13,198
[Julio] <i>Where is your mother?</i>

20
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:15,075
<i>I thought she was dropping by for dinner.</i>

21
00:01:15,158 --> 00:01:17,702
<i>I'm not expecting this family</i>
<i>to ever become whole again.</i>

22
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:18,661
<i>Mama doesn't need you.</i>

23
00:01:18,745 --> 00:01:21,206
<i>Just because I'm not governor right now,</i>

24
00:01:21,289 --> 00:01:23,333
<i>doesn't mean you can</i>
<i>treat me like an old rag!</i>

25
00:01:23,416 --> 00:01:25,084
[Romulo] <i>Go ahead, Jaguar. Load it up.</i>

26
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:27,378
<i>Come back with</i>
<i>the money at exactly 10:00 p.m.</i>

27
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:29,506
<i>Make sure it's the exact amount.</i>

28
00:01:29,589 --> 00:01:30,381
[Romulo] <i>I'll go with you.</i>

29
00:01:30,465 --> 00:01:32,175
<i>You don't know where to deliver the goods.</i>

30
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:33,134
<i>Just leave it to me.</i>

31
00:01:33,218 --> 00:01:36,596
<i>-If you really know, tell us.</i>
<i>-That's not necessary.</i>

32
00:01:36,679 --> 00:01:38,348
<i>You know what to do with him.</i>

33
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:41,559
<i>Don't let him escape!</i>

34
00:01:42,894 --> 00:01:44,521
<i>Oh, here's an update.</i>

35
00:01:44,604 --> 00:01:47,190
-[phone ringing]
-[Lily] <i>Didn't we say no phones?</i>

36
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:49,192
<i>We said no such things.</i>

37
00:01:49,275 --> 00:01:52,237
<i>You can ignore your own daughter,</i>

38
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:53,404
<i>but not me.</i>

39
00:01:53,488 --> 00:01:54,948
<i>Not me.</i>

40
00:01:57,951 --> 00:01:59,035
Then, who?

41
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:00,578
[tense music playing]

42
00:02:01,704 --> 00:02:03,456
[laughs]

43
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,253
Never mind.

44
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:15,510
[grunts]

45
00:02:38,074 --> 00:02:38,950
[groans]

46
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:58,136
But I did notice that Emilia's
insecurities are getting worse.

47
00:02:58,219 --> 00:03:01,389
Maybe you need to give her some attention.

48
00:03:01,973 --> 00:03:05,602
I don't think I'm closer to you
than I am to my daughter.

49
00:03:06,311 --> 00:03:09,439
Believe me or not, I'm just concerned.

50
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:12,150
[phone chimes]

51
00:03:12,859 --> 00:03:13,776
[gasps]

52
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:15,486
IT'S DONE.

53
00:03:16,237 --> 00:03:17,238
[sighs]

54
00:03:21,284 --> 00:03:22,201
No phones.

55
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:23,244
[chuckles]

56
00:03:24,078 --> 00:03:27,999
But, like what you said,
you're not young anymore.

57
00:03:28,082 --> 00:03:31,711
And you have other matters
to attend to, right?

58
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:38,927
Well then. Um… Let's call it a night.

59
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:40,970
Yes.

60
00:03:42,513 --> 00:03:44,224
Good night, Mama.

61
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:46,100
Good night, Lily.

62
00:03:46,893 --> 00:03:48,895
[suspenseful music playing]

63
00:04:10,708 --> 00:04:12,710
[birds chirping]

64
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:17,215
What's this? Why is there a truck here?

65
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:20,009
Sir!

66
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:22,220
There's a truck blocking the way.

67
00:04:23,179 --> 00:04:24,347
Let's check it out.

68
00:04:26,808 --> 00:04:28,059
Red Dragon?

69
00:04:32,063 --> 00:04:33,106
It's unlocked.

70
00:04:33,439 --> 00:04:35,900
Toledo! Tabang! Hurry and open this truck!

71
00:04:40,446 --> 00:04:42,448
[locks clicking]

72
00:04:47,120 --> 00:04:48,246
Check those boxes.

73
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:52,166
Sir, these are guns!

74
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:54,794
Check everything! Check everything!

75
00:05:04,262 --> 00:05:06,973
[Lily] Were you able to bring
the shipment to the police?

76
00:05:07,598 --> 00:05:09,350
The shipment is in
the police's custody now.

77
00:05:09,851 --> 00:05:11,102
[Diego] <i>And soon enough…</i>

78
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:12,729
they'll be raiding the warehouse.

79
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:14,772
Lily, I also found something

80
00:05:14,856 --> 00:05:16,983
that we can use against Red Dragon.

81
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:21,154
That would be a big help
to taking Helena Montoya down.

82
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:25,783
But Diego, how did you do it?

83
00:05:28,786 --> 00:05:32,540
What did you do to get
into Red Dragon's hideout?

84
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:39,088
You'll find out soon. For now,
the important thing is,

85
00:05:39,172 --> 00:05:41,090
<i>we take Red Dragon down.</i>

86
00:05:53,227 --> 00:05:55,021
[tense music playing]

87
00:06:24,008 --> 00:06:25,343
Sir, positive!

88
00:06:27,678 --> 00:06:30,014
[Angelie on TV] <i>More than a</i>
<i>thousand guns, including rifles</i>

89
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:34,102
<i>and other firearms amounting</i>
<i>to over 50 million pesos</i>

90
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:39,107
<i>are in police custody after being seized</i>
<i>from a shipment made by Red Dragon.</i>

91
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:43,027
<i>As of now, the police are trying to unmask</i>
<i>the identity of Red Dragon,</i>

92
00:06:43,111 --> 00:06:46,364
<i>who is facing charges</i>
<i>of illegal arms trade and trafficking.</i>

93
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:50,576
<i>It can be recalled that Red Dragon is</i>
<i>also wanted for child prostitution.</i>

94
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:53,079
[infuriated scream]

95
00:06:57,458 --> 00:07:00,044
[screaming]

96
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:05,007
Now, the police know that
Red Dragon is active

97
00:07:05,091 --> 00:07:07,593
not just here in Ardiente,
but in the whole country.

98
00:07:07,677 --> 00:07:11,097
Mom, it's not enough
that the shipment was sabotaged.

99
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:13,766
The woman behind it needs to pay.

100
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:17,311
Helena Montoya must pay.

101
00:07:21,315 --> 00:07:23,109
-[panting]
-[Mercedes] Madam.

102
00:07:23,192 --> 00:07:26,946
Madam, it was an inside job.
I'll prove it to you.

103
00:07:28,030 --> 00:07:30,032
[slow tense music playing]

104
00:07:36,914 --> 00:07:39,000
Prove what? That it's you?

105
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:43,546
You're the reason the shipment failed!

106
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:49,302
Mercedes, you know how
many people this pin has killed.

107
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:54,640
Madam, please! It wasn't me!

108
00:07:55,683 --> 00:07:59,937
It was Jaguar.
The Jaguar double-crossed us.

109
00:08:00,646 --> 00:08:03,357
[dramatic music playing]

110
00:08:14,952 --> 00:08:18,539
[Lily] I'll expose Helena Montoya.

111
00:08:18,831 --> 00:08:22,668
I'll reveal that she's Red Dragon.

112
00:08:23,377 --> 00:08:27,340
After what Diego did,
I'll release the documents

113
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:29,550
I got out of Mercedes Palacio's laptop.

114
00:08:29,634 --> 00:08:32,178
The evidence you got from Club Dragonfly

115
00:08:32,261 --> 00:08:34,013
will also help the case.

116
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:35,932
That's right, Mom.

117
00:08:36,557 --> 00:08:41,938
And we need a witness to catch
Helena Montoya in the act.

118
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:44,899
[suspenseful music playing]

119
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:48,569
She forgets that gold can change form.

120
00:08:49,779 --> 00:08:54,367
It gets even harder when exposed to fire.

121
00:08:56,661 --> 00:08:58,955
So bring it on, Helena Montoya.

122
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:03,417
Let's see how great Red Dragon really is.

123
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:07,588
Because I'm here to slay you.

124
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:09,590
[tense music playing]

125
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:23,437
The Jaguar betrayed me?

126
00:09:41,956 --> 00:09:42,707
[grunts]

127
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:56,846
[slow tense music playing]

128
00:10:01,225 --> 00:10:04,353
Find the Jaguar! Now!

129
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:16,907
Didn't I tell you never to call me here?

130
00:10:17,366 --> 00:10:19,493
[Damian's henchman]
<i>But, Boss, we have a problem.</i>

131
00:10:19,577 --> 00:10:22,580
<i>The shipment was raided last night.</i>

132
00:10:22,955 --> 00:10:25,833
<i>The police have our guns.</i>
<i>It's on the news.</i>

133
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:36,886
[henchman] <i>I'm sure</i>
<i>Red Dragon's pissed right now.</i>

134
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:40,222
<i>Knowing her, whoever failed her</i>
<i>will be burned alive.</i>

135
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:45,436
[panting]

136
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:05,247
What were you thinking?
Why'd you wear that mask?

137
00:11:05,831 --> 00:11:07,541
I went to Red Dragon's hideout

138
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:10,503
so I could stop their operations.

139
00:11:12,963 --> 00:11:14,465
Do you know what you're doing?

140
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:17,927
Do you hear yourself, Diego?
You think this is right?!

141
00:11:18,469 --> 00:11:21,055
Sorry for putting your life
in danger, Dad.

142
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:25,893
But no matter what happens,
I'll do whatever it takes

143
00:11:26,477 --> 00:11:29,605
to stop Red Dragon and all her plans.

144
00:11:29,688 --> 00:11:30,773
[scoffs]

145
00:11:31,732 --> 00:11:33,609
Don't worry about me, son.

146
00:11:34,276 --> 00:11:35,945
You should worry about yourself.

147
00:11:36,946 --> 00:11:39,115
After what you did, she'll
definitely come after you.

148
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:52,253
[ominous music playing]

149
00:12:04,348 --> 00:12:06,350
[grunting]

150
00:12:12,940 --> 00:12:14,024
[engine starts]

151
00:12:29,623 --> 00:12:34,086
Madam Red Dragon,
I had nothing to do with that.

152
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,505
Don't lie to me.

153
00:12:39,258 --> 00:12:43,471
If I'd been behind that mask,
would I come back here?

154
00:12:46,599 --> 00:12:50,686
If that were the case,
shouldn't I be hiding from you?

155
00:12:52,813 --> 00:12:56,525
I'm telling you,
I didn't sabotage the shipment.

156
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:02,072
If that wasn't you, then who was it?

157
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:06,243
Who?!

158
00:13:09,079 --> 00:13:14,793
An imposter who goes around
and calls himself the Jaguar.

159
00:13:18,506 --> 00:13:20,633
He was the one
who sabotaged your shipment.

160
00:13:23,344 --> 00:13:25,346
Get out. Everybody get out!

161
00:13:39,193 --> 00:13:40,402
[Helena] <i>Hello. Finally.</i>

162
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:42,238
<i>Mercedes, I can't reach you</i>
<i>on your cellphone.</i>

163
00:13:42,321 --> 00:13:45,074
<i>I've been trying to call you.</i>
<i>You need to report to me, ASAP.</i>

164
00:13:45,658 --> 00:13:48,327
[Helena] <i>Hello, Mercedes. Can you hear me?</i>

165
00:13:49,703 --> 00:13:52,831
<i>Then tell me. Who answered the phone?</i>

166
00:13:53,624 --> 00:13:54,875
<i>Were you with someone?</i>

167
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:56,710
<i>Yes, Madam.</i>

168
00:13:56,794 --> 00:14:02,007
<i>And I did not answer because I was wasted.</i>

169
00:14:04,635 --> 00:14:07,972
<i>You're the reason why the shipment failed!</i>

170
00:14:08,055 --> 00:14:11,475
<i>It wasn't me. It was Jaguar.</i>

171
00:14:11,559 --> 00:14:14,186
[Mercedes] <i>The Jaguar double-crossed us.</i>

172
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:15,771
<i>I had nothing to do with that.</i>

173
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:20,317
<i>An imposter who goes around</i>
<i>and calls himself the Jaguar.</i>

174
00:14:23,612 --> 00:14:25,072
<i>-Helena!</i>
<i>-It's different to me.</i>

175
00:14:25,155 --> 00:14:28,200
[Emilia] <i>It's not just an act of kindness</i>
<i>that you see in Lily Cruz.</i>

176
00:14:28,284 --> 00:14:29,869
<i>You know what she did to me before, Mama?</i>

177
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:32,204
<i>She almost took a bullet for my life.</i>

178
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:34,498
<i>She saved my life. Exactly the same thing</i>

179
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,041
<i>that she's doing to you right now, Mama.</i>

180
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:40,421
<i>See what kind of person</i>
<i>our little "friend" is?</i>

181
00:14:43,215 --> 00:14:45,092
I have three people of interest.

182
00:14:45,175 --> 00:14:47,011
[tense music playing]

183
00:14:47,094 --> 00:14:47,887
Mercedes.

184
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:49,096
Damian.

185
00:14:49,805 --> 00:14:51,390
Lily Cruz.

186
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:58,188
And I know how to hit
all of them at the same time.

187
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:05,446
Diego.

188
00:15:07,031 --> 00:15:07,781
Lily.

189
00:15:10,659 --> 00:15:13,579
I'm sure Red Dragon
is looking for the person

190
00:15:13,662 --> 00:15:15,414
who sabotaged her operation.

191
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:17,958
So please, be careful.

192
00:15:24,089 --> 00:15:25,758
I think I made a mistake, Lily.

193
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,096
I pretended to be someone else

194
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:33,682
to infiltrate Red Dragon's hideout.

195
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:40,940
And because of that,
someone else might get hurt.

196
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,947
But you know me, Lily.

197
00:15:49,698 --> 00:15:53,702
My whole life,
I've fought for what's right.

198
00:15:55,079 --> 00:15:57,081
This is the only time
I've lied and stole--

199
00:15:57,164 --> 00:15:59,416
Diego, wait, what are you talking about?

200
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,212
Sometimes, you have to do things…

201
00:16:04,421 --> 00:16:06,006
you don't want to for the greater good.

202
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:12,596
I wish… I wish I'd done this sooner.

203
00:16:14,723 --> 00:16:16,725
[pensive music playing]

204
00:16:36,120 --> 00:16:39,123
I may not know what you're talking about,

205
00:16:41,083 --> 00:16:44,837
but don't ever think
you're wrong for fighting

206
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:47,339
for what's right.

207
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:56,640
Diego, I've always admired you
for fighting for the truth.

208
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:59,852
I know you're a man of principles.

209
00:17:00,185 --> 00:17:04,398
And, that's why I hope you never change.

210
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:06,942
I hope you never lose that integrity.

211
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:21,707
Damian, come here. Try this.

212
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:23,751
It's been Lily's favorite
since she was a kid.

213
00:17:24,209 --> 00:17:26,045
I bet you'll like it too.

214
00:17:26,545 --> 00:17:27,880
Yeah. It does look good.

215
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:32,676
Dig in.

216
00:17:43,937 --> 00:17:47,399
Are you still thinking about
Red Dragon's failed operation?

217
00:17:49,151 --> 00:17:51,695
Who do you think
could've foiled her plans?

218
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:02,915
Maybe it's one of her
own minions in the syndicate.

219
00:18:03,957 --> 00:18:05,918
One of Red Dragon's minions?

220
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:16,637
Mom?

221
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:19,014
-Lily. Diego.
-Auntie.

222
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:20,349
You're just in time.

223
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:21,892
I just finished making some snacks.

224
00:18:21,975 --> 00:18:23,018
-Wow!
-Come join us.

225
00:18:23,102 --> 00:18:25,020
Sure. Diego and I are a bit hungry.

226
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:26,146
[phone ringing]

227
00:18:27,356 --> 00:18:28,774
Sorry, hold on.

228
00:18:30,025 --> 00:18:31,193
It's the dragon.

229
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:33,821
Helena?

230
00:18:34,279 --> 00:18:35,239
Hi, Lily.

231
00:18:35,697 --> 00:18:37,324
Yes. Need anything?

232
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:40,327
I called to invite you
to another bonding session.

233
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:42,412
I felt like the other night
ended too early.

234
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:47,793
Oh. I thought I was the only
one who thought that.

235
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:52,840
Well, I did say you could call
whenever you needed me.

236
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:57,636
So, what do you have in mind? Dinner?

237
00:18:59,221 --> 00:19:00,514
Better.

238
00:19:01,056 --> 00:19:03,058
[suspenseful music playing]

239
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:14,611
Oh, hey Anna.

240
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:16,697
So, did you tell Jepoy you love him?

241
00:19:17,614 --> 00:19:21,535
I'm too afraid to tell him.
I don't want to get hurt.

242
00:19:23,203 --> 00:19:25,205
Anna, relax. Being in love isn't wrong.

243
00:19:26,790 --> 00:19:28,125
Why? Have you ever been in love?

244
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:29,835
I hope so.

245
00:19:30,711 --> 00:19:32,963
I mean, it feels so good to be in love.

246
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:38,343
Especially when you're
with the one who matters.

247
00:19:40,095 --> 00:19:42,639
Just the two of you, talking…

248
00:19:45,601 --> 00:19:46,894
laughing…

249
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:54,443
Just being together.
Holding each other, embracing.

250
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:57,696
Hugging them tight.

251
00:19:57,946 --> 00:19:59,031
[ominous music playing]

252
00:20:00,324 --> 00:20:02,201
You hold them tight, because…

253
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:05,245
you always want them by your side.

254
00:20:07,414 --> 00:20:09,082
And, you'll hug them even tighter

255
00:20:09,166 --> 00:20:10,709
so that they'll never leave.

256
00:20:12,085 --> 00:20:14,296
You'll keep them with
you because they're yours.

257
00:20:14,379 --> 00:20:15,547
[chokes] Arnaldo.

258
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:19,468
They're all yours and you don't
want anyone else to have them!

259
00:20:19,551 --> 00:20:20,719
Stop it Arnaldo!

260
00:20:23,222 --> 00:20:24,848
Why were you trying to choke me?!

261
00:20:24,932 --> 00:20:26,391
[tense music playing]

262
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:28,227
No, I…

263
00:20:36,068 --> 00:20:39,571
[panting]

264
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:00,842
[tense music playing]

265
00:21:14,648 --> 00:21:15,774
We're done, ma'am.

266
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:17,067
Thank you.

267
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:22,656
I told you my masseuse
was fabulous, right?

268
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:23,949
[ominous music playing]

269
00:21:34,876 --> 00:21:35,919
Helena?

270
00:21:37,754 --> 00:21:39,339
Do you know what this is?

271
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:42,718
[Lily] Ah!

272
00:21:43,802 --> 00:21:48,390
It could be painful but
it could also give you pleasure.

273
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:53,937
It could also be deadly.

274
00:21:55,480 --> 00:21:57,357
Especially if you prick

275
00:21:57,441 --> 00:22:03,322
the death spot at the back of the neck.

276
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:12,706
It would lead to oxygen
deprivation, and then, death.

277
00:22:31,391 --> 00:22:39,232
So, Lily, why don't we play a little game?

278
00:22:41,943 --> 00:22:46,406
All you have to do is answer
as truthfully as you can.

279
00:22:47,407 --> 00:22:48,617
Are you ready?

280
00:22:52,954 --> 00:22:54,956
Can I trust you?

281
00:22:57,334 --> 00:22:58,085
Ouch!

282
00:22:59,544 --> 00:23:00,420
Yes!

283
00:23:01,505 --> 00:23:02,923
Do you trust me?

284
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:05,300
Or are you wary of me?

285
00:23:13,517 --> 00:23:15,060
Are we really friends?

286
00:23:19,356 --> 00:23:20,482
Helena.

287
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:24,486
If we really are friends…

288
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:31,952
are you willing to risk
your life for a friend?

289
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:34,454
[suspenseful music playing]

290
00:23:51,096 --> 00:23:52,055
Ah!

291
00:23:53,765 --> 00:23:55,392
Ouch. [chuckling]

292
00:23:55,725 --> 00:23:57,727
Lily, I was just kidding.

293
00:23:58,728 --> 00:23:59,771
Kidding?

294
00:24:01,731 --> 00:24:02,482
Hmm.

295
00:24:02,899 --> 00:24:05,902
You're just like your daughter, Emilia.

296
00:24:06,570 --> 00:24:07,904
Well then Mama,

297
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:12,951
the answer to all your
questions is a solid yes.

298
00:24:13,326 --> 00:24:17,706
Because I know the person I'm talking to

299
00:24:17,956 --> 00:24:20,041
isn't hiding anything from me.

300
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:21,960
Right, Mama?

301
00:24:22,335 --> 00:24:24,379
Right?! Mama!

302
00:24:25,130 --> 00:24:27,924
[suspenseful music playing]

303
00:24:31,720 --> 00:24:32,846
Say yes.

304
00:24:38,143 --> 00:24:39,102
Yes.

305
00:24:40,604 --> 00:24:42,189
Very good, Mama.

306
00:24:43,231 --> 00:24:44,357
You know what, Mama?

307
00:24:45,025 --> 00:24:49,905
I have eyes watching you
even when I'm away.

308
00:24:49,988 --> 00:24:52,115
I already know about your plans,

309
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:54,451
even before you come up with them.

310
00:24:55,660 --> 00:24:57,662
So, don't you even dare, Mama.

311
00:25:13,136 --> 00:25:15,138
[tense music playing]

312
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:23,813
Are you okay, Mama?

313
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:25,523
-Yeah.
-Let me help you.

314
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:33,740
Hmm… So relaxing.

315
00:25:42,582 --> 00:25:44,501
[Lily] I've spoken to
Attorney Fisher, Mom.

316
00:25:44,584 --> 00:25:47,587
There's an investigator
on Helena Montoya's trail.

317
00:25:48,171 --> 00:25:49,422
What do you think?

318
00:25:49,506 --> 00:25:51,716
Do you think she knows that
you're aware of her true identity?

319
00:25:54,010 --> 00:25:58,139
It doesn't matter, Mom.
But she can't kill me

320
00:25:58,223 --> 00:26:01,268
because I'm the one
who keeps her name clean.

321
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:03,103
Lily, what are you planning?

322
00:26:04,604 --> 00:26:06,398
The fight continues, Mom.

323
00:26:07,065 --> 00:26:11,319
But this time, I'll stick
even closer to that woman

324
00:26:11,695 --> 00:26:13,863
until I catch her in the act.

325
00:26:19,869 --> 00:26:20,787
Mama.

326
00:26:22,789 --> 00:26:25,000
How was your bonding with Lily Cruz?

327
00:26:25,083 --> 00:26:27,085
Am I going to have someone buried soon?

328
00:26:27,752 --> 00:26:32,549
Yes, but not Lily. She's still an asset.

329
00:26:32,924 --> 00:26:37,012
And we can't just kill her
without sufficient proof

330
00:26:37,095 --> 00:26:39,264
that she's involved in the sabotage.

331
00:26:41,558 --> 00:26:42,934
How about Jaguar?

332
00:26:43,810 --> 00:26:45,645
He's the one on the CCTV footage.

333
00:26:45,729 --> 00:26:47,522
Should we really believe what he said?

334
00:26:47,605 --> 00:26:50,525
That an imposter took the shipment?

335
00:26:51,484 --> 00:26:52,402
Wait, Mama.

336
00:26:52,485 --> 00:26:55,280
Are you trying to say
that Jaguar is now a suspect?

337
00:26:56,239 --> 00:26:56,990
Yes.

338
00:26:58,158 --> 00:27:02,203
Mercedes, find someone skilled enough

339
00:27:03,163 --> 00:27:04,664
to take care of the Jaguar.

340
00:27:05,957 --> 00:27:07,208
Wait, Mama.

341
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:09,753
Jaguar is my friend.

342
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:13,965
Yes, Mama, he's been my long-time friend

343
00:27:14,049 --> 00:27:16,217
and he was there for me
during my dark days.

344
00:27:16,301 --> 00:27:19,971
So, please. Mama, don't hurt him.

345
00:27:21,973 --> 00:27:23,767
Are we talking about the same Jaguar?

346
00:27:27,395 --> 00:27:28,438
[Diego] <i>Dad.</i>

347
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:30,940
[crickets chirping]

348
00:27:31,566 --> 00:27:33,526
I'm glad we got to spend time together.

349
00:27:36,071 --> 00:27:37,238
And thank you.

350
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:44,162
Thank you for always protecting me.

351
00:27:44,245 --> 00:27:46,247
[pensive music playing]

352
00:27:47,999 --> 00:27:49,125
I always will, son.

353
00:27:51,294 --> 00:27:53,963
Thank you too for saving my life.

354
00:27:57,008 --> 00:27:58,510
But please…

355
00:28:00,553 --> 00:28:03,098
I don't want you wearing this mask again.

356
00:28:03,848 --> 00:28:06,059
-But, Dad…
-This isn't for you, son.

357
00:28:06,810 --> 00:28:08,520
I can use it for the greater good

358
00:28:08,895 --> 00:28:10,772
and to take down Red Dragon.

359
00:28:11,564 --> 00:28:13,733
If Red Dragon's all you're worried about,

360
00:28:14,150 --> 00:28:19,364
fine, I'll help you.
I'll help you investigate her.

361
00:28:20,365 --> 00:28:23,034
But like I said,
don't ever use this again.

362
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:24,828
Do you understand?

363
00:28:34,129 --> 00:28:36,172
Mama, my friend, Jaguar, told me that

364
00:28:36,256 --> 00:28:39,217
there are two Jaguars.
One of them is a copycat.

365
00:28:39,551 --> 00:28:43,221
Yes, but I'm pretty sure
that the Jaguar I know

366
00:28:43,763 --> 00:28:44,889
is the real one.

367
00:28:46,641 --> 00:28:47,475
[sighs]

368
00:28:48,977 --> 00:28:52,439
So, instead of investigating Lily,

369
00:28:52,981 --> 00:28:56,443
why don't you try to investigate
your Jaguar friend?

370
00:28:58,611 --> 00:29:01,906
Okay, Mama.
I will talk to my Jaguar friend.

371
00:29:02,615 --> 00:29:06,453
But please, don't stop me
from investigating Lily Cruz.

372
00:29:06,703 --> 00:29:08,621
I know that woman very well.

373
00:29:08,955 --> 00:29:11,958
She has messed up
my family countless times.

374
00:29:12,041 --> 00:29:14,461
And I don't want the same thing
to happen to you, Mama.

375
00:29:16,004 --> 00:29:17,297
Do we have a deal now?

376
00:29:18,590 --> 00:29:20,258
Yes, we have a deal.

377
00:29:24,179 --> 00:29:27,265
Lily, please don't take this
the wrong way…

378
00:29:29,309 --> 00:29:33,313
but isn't there another way
to take Helena Montoya down?

379
00:29:36,566 --> 00:29:37,817
Mom…

380
00:29:40,779 --> 00:29:43,114
Do you want me
to stop getting close to her?

381
00:29:44,407 --> 00:29:45,784
Lily, I'm trying.

382
00:29:48,453 --> 00:29:54,125
But I can't forget how the
Ardientes captured you before.

383
00:29:56,419 --> 00:29:58,755
That won't ever happen again, Mom.

384
00:30:00,215 --> 00:30:02,133
I always take care of myself

385
00:30:02,217 --> 00:30:04,177
because I don't want us
to be separated again.

386
00:30:04,969 --> 00:30:07,639
Because your life
is as important as mine, Mom.

387
00:30:08,014 --> 00:30:10,391
So, I'm taking care of myself.

388
00:30:12,143 --> 00:30:14,270
I promise I'll always be careful.

389
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:17,732
[phone chimes]

390
00:30:22,529 --> 00:30:26,241
I HAVE PROOF THAT HELENA MONTOYA
IS RED DRAGON.

391
00:30:31,371 --> 00:30:32,872
Is something wrong?

392
00:30:34,999 --> 00:30:36,835
It's an anonymous text, Mom.

393
00:30:38,545 --> 00:30:41,923
It says they have proof
Helena Montoya is Red Dragon.

394
00:30:50,932 --> 00:30:54,519
<i>Red Dragon's identity remains</i>
<i>a mystery to the public.</i>

395
00:30:54,602 --> 00:30:55,770
<i>She's allegedly connected</i>
<i>to child prostitution--</i>

396
00:30:55,854 --> 00:30:56,938
Red Dragon.

397
00:30:57,021 --> 00:30:59,023
<i>…and illegal trafficking</i>
<i>of high-powered arms.</i>

398
00:30:59,107 --> 00:31:05,697
Jaguar. Why didn't I think
of an alias for myself?

399
00:31:06,948 --> 00:31:09,993
What would be a cheesy, nice alias?

400
00:31:11,411 --> 00:31:13,162
The Roaring Lion.

401
00:31:15,957 --> 00:31:17,125
The Kingpin.

402
00:31:18,293 --> 00:31:19,961
The Leviathan.

403
00:31:21,296 --> 00:31:22,505
Killer Shark.

404
00:31:25,258 --> 00:31:27,844
Handsome Devil.

405
00:31:29,429 --> 00:31:30,471
Nah.

406
00:31:31,055 --> 00:31:33,224
Sounds too narcissistic.

407
00:31:34,017 --> 00:31:36,311
<i>Reports say that even</i>
<i>the police find it difficult</i>

408
00:31:36,394 --> 00:31:37,979
<i>to chase down the said criminal.</i>

409
00:31:38,062 --> 00:31:41,316
<i>Everyone is advised to remain</i>
<i>vigilant against the</i>

410
00:31:41,399 --> 00:31:44,068
<i>group's modus operandi,</i>
<i>which is said to be rampant.</i>

411
00:31:44,319 --> 00:31:46,529
<i>This is Angelie Berlin, reporting.</i>

412
00:31:48,656 --> 00:31:49,574
[scoffs]

413
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:53,286
I got news for you, news people.

414
00:31:54,203 --> 00:31:56,831
I haven't just been beside her.

415
00:31:58,124 --> 00:32:00,835
I've even slept with the enemy.

416
00:32:01,586 --> 00:32:03,171
And she found me delicious.

417
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:05,590
[laughing]

418
00:32:07,967 --> 00:32:11,179
Oh my, Helena.

419
00:32:13,097 --> 00:32:14,307
You're a puzzle.

420
00:32:16,142 --> 00:32:17,101
Sir.

421
00:32:17,185 --> 00:32:18,144
-Yeah?
-You have a visitor.

422
00:32:18,227 --> 00:32:20,939
Missing me already, Julio Ardiente?

423
00:32:21,940 --> 00:32:23,942
[tense music playing]

424
00:32:28,363 --> 00:32:31,199
Helena, what do you want?

425
00:32:31,282 --> 00:32:33,743
Why are you here in my house again?

426
00:32:33,826 --> 00:32:37,664
Emilia told me you were asking
her when I was available.

427
00:32:38,456 --> 00:32:41,125
Well, I'm available now.

428
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:46,506
I must admit I missed you.

429
00:32:47,757 --> 00:32:50,218
Although, I'm not prepared now.

430
00:32:51,010 --> 00:32:52,345
You know when I was prepared?

431
00:32:52,428 --> 00:32:53,471
[jazz music playing]

432
00:32:53,930 --> 00:32:59,644
A couple of days ago.
When you didn't show up.

433
00:33:00,520 --> 00:33:02,355
Before you get any ideas,

434
00:33:02,438 --> 00:33:04,524
I thought this is just a friendly meeting.

435
00:33:04,607 --> 00:33:05,942
Well, I'm here now.

436
00:33:06,442 --> 00:33:07,735
But you know what?

437
00:33:07,819 --> 00:33:11,155
I'm feeling tired. So, I'm going to bed.

438
00:33:12,281 --> 00:33:14,993
You're sleeping over?

439
00:33:15,076 --> 00:33:17,245
Yeah. Why? Is there a problem?

440
00:33:17,870 --> 00:33:22,000
No, no, no. I can have
the maids change my bedsheets.

441
00:33:22,375 --> 00:33:23,418
Satin pink.

442
00:33:23,918 --> 00:33:26,921
Don't be silly. I'm going
to be using the guest room.

443
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:29,090
In fact, my bags are already there.

444
00:33:29,173 --> 00:33:32,176
The guest room is musky, Helena.

445
00:33:33,428 --> 00:33:34,429
Really?

446
00:33:34,512 --> 00:33:36,431
-Yes.
-It's musky?

447
00:33:37,432 --> 00:33:42,645
Then I better take a shower
so that I will stay fresh.

448
00:33:45,815 --> 00:33:48,026
-Goodnight.
-The shower's in my room.

449
00:33:48,109 --> 00:33:49,944
It's big, it's large, it's sexy.

450
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:51,946
I'm still staying in the guest room.

451
00:33:52,030 --> 00:33:55,867
Good night, Julio. You silly old cow.

452
00:33:57,702 --> 00:34:01,205
-Silly old cow, my foot!
-[door closes]

453
00:34:03,291 --> 00:34:05,376
Who could the sender be?

454
00:34:05,835 --> 00:34:09,380
Who else knows that you know that
Red Dragon and Helena Montoya

455
00:34:09,464 --> 00:34:10,506
are the same person?

456
00:34:11,632 --> 00:34:13,968
It's nice to know there's a helping hand.

457
00:34:15,970 --> 00:34:17,889
Though I have no idea who that person is.

458
00:34:17,972 --> 00:34:22,435
But don't worry, Mom.
I'll figure this one out.

459
00:34:23,144 --> 00:34:26,314
I'll get back to you.
For now, you should rest.

460
00:34:27,148 --> 00:34:28,524
Okay, then.

461
00:34:30,777 --> 00:34:32,111
-Good night, Mom.
-Good night.

462
00:34:42,872 --> 00:34:44,999
I HAVE PROOF THAT HELENA MONTOYA
IS RED DRAGON.

463
00:34:53,007 --> 00:34:55,009
Raul couldn't have done it.

464
00:34:56,135 --> 00:34:57,178
[suspenseful music playing]

465
00:34:57,261 --> 00:34:59,597
The last time I saw him,
he was shot in the stomach.

466
00:35:00,598 --> 00:35:02,058
[Damian] <i>I'll deal with that impostor!</i>

467
00:35:06,562 --> 00:35:09,107
But the Jaguar on the CCTV footage

468
00:35:09,190 --> 00:35:10,817
didn't look like he was injured.

469
00:35:19,033 --> 00:35:22,203
[suspenseful music playing]

470
00:35:27,875 --> 00:35:29,544
-[grunts]
-[gunshots]

471
00:35:29,627 --> 00:35:31,003
[Raul] <i>Let Diego go!</i>

472
00:35:33,089 --> 00:35:34,549
<i>Diego, run!</i>

473
00:35:36,634 --> 00:35:37,885
[Damian] <i>I said, leave!</i>

474
00:35:43,599 --> 00:35:44,976
It's Diego.

475
00:35:46,769 --> 00:35:49,313
Diego's pretending to be Jaguar.

476
00:35:52,859 --> 00:35:54,902
[music swells]

477
00:35:57,196 --> 00:35:59,574
-Nanny! Uncle!
-Oh! Diego!

478
00:35:59,657 --> 00:36:01,617
-Nanny!
-Pandoy, Diego's here!

479
00:36:01,951 --> 00:36:03,870
[Pandoy] Diego? Diego! Diego, son!

480
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:05,538
-Uncle!
-Diego, how are you?

481
00:36:05,621 --> 00:36:06,622
Uncle!

482
00:36:08,624 --> 00:36:09,500
Oh, my.

483
00:36:09,584 --> 00:36:11,377
-Diego, what happened?
-You've been gone for days!

484
00:36:11,460 --> 00:36:12,628
How are you?

485
00:36:12,712 --> 00:36:14,297
-Right.
-What happened to you, Diego?

486
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:17,967
Good thing Lily always tells us
what you're up to.

487
00:36:18,050 --> 00:36:20,553
Otherwise, your aunt
would've been so worried.

488
00:36:21,220 --> 00:36:25,600
Nanny, Uncle, I told you
not to worry about me.

489
00:36:26,142 --> 00:36:27,435
I can take care of myself.

490
00:36:28,394 --> 00:36:29,187
[Loring laughs]

491
00:36:29,270 --> 00:36:30,897
I just had to take care of something.

492
00:36:31,355 --> 00:36:32,481
What?

493
00:36:35,443 --> 00:36:37,486
Good morning, Mrs. Loring.

494
00:36:37,987 --> 00:36:39,614
Good morning.

495
00:36:43,701 --> 00:36:45,786
Dad, I know you didn't approve
of what I did.

496
00:36:47,622 --> 00:36:51,918
But I want you to know
that I don't regret it.

497
00:36:55,588 --> 00:36:58,716
Son, you don't have to explain anything.

498
00:36:59,592 --> 00:37:00,843
I understand.

499
00:37:02,136 --> 00:37:04,180
And I respect your decision.

500
00:37:05,848 --> 00:37:07,975
I'm just here to support you.

501
00:37:08,893 --> 00:37:09,936
Thanks, Dad.

502
00:37:13,648 --> 00:37:16,484
[Loring and Pandoy laugh]

503
00:37:16,567 --> 00:37:18,736
We have no idea what you're talking about.

504
00:37:18,819 --> 00:37:20,071
Yep. She's right.

505
00:37:20,821 --> 00:37:22,823
It looks like they're getting along.

506
00:37:23,282 --> 00:37:28,037
If you're happy, Diego, then
Pandoy and I are happy for you.

507
00:37:28,120 --> 00:37:29,580
That's true.
We may not get what's going on,

508
00:37:29,664 --> 00:37:31,249
but I guess it sounded like a good thing.

509
00:37:31,332 --> 00:37:32,458
[Loring and Pandoy laughing]

510
00:37:32,541 --> 00:37:34,710
Nanny, I'm always happy when I'm with you.

511
00:37:35,503 --> 00:37:37,171
I've missed you so much.

512
00:37:37,255 --> 00:37:38,673
-We missed you too.
-Come here, you two.

513
00:37:38,756 --> 00:37:39,632
[Pandoy laughing]

514
00:37:41,550 --> 00:37:43,177
You have such a bright smile on you.

515
00:37:43,261 --> 00:37:45,596
[Emilia] <i>So you're the fake Jaguar?</i>

516
00:37:45,680 --> 00:37:48,307
I need to speak to you. Answer the phone!

517
00:37:48,391 --> 00:37:49,433
[line ringing]

518
00:37:51,852 --> 00:37:54,563
This is really important.
I need you to pick up the phone.

519
00:37:54,647 --> 00:37:55,523
[line ringing]

520
00:37:55,606 --> 00:37:56,899
[grunts]

521
00:37:59,110 --> 00:38:01,654
Raul. Don't tell me you just got home.

522
00:38:03,948 --> 00:38:06,033
Well, so much for you acting like a wife.

523
00:38:06,534 --> 00:38:10,579
I've been gone for days
and you just noticed?

524
00:38:10,663 --> 00:38:13,207
Wait, did Mama see you?

525
00:38:13,874 --> 00:38:15,251
Your mother's here?

526
00:38:15,334 --> 00:38:17,837
Yeah. And she cannot see you like this.

527
00:38:17,920 --> 00:38:19,588
You need to take a bath.
You need to shave.

528
00:38:19,672 --> 00:38:23,301
Oh my God, you need to take a shower.
She cannot see you like this, Raul.

529
00:38:27,096 --> 00:38:28,597
Good morning, Julio.

530
00:38:29,765 --> 00:38:33,853
It is indeed a beautiful morning.

531
00:38:33,936 --> 00:38:35,062
Did you sleep well?

532
00:38:35,146 --> 00:38:38,858
Not as much as I would've loved to.

533
00:38:38,941 --> 00:38:43,195
But it is indeed a beautiful morning.

534
00:38:45,990 --> 00:38:51,746
You know what would really be
an ideal good morning

535
00:38:51,829 --> 00:38:53,372
for the two of us?

536
00:38:55,583 --> 00:39:00,504
It's us not having to come
out of different rooms

537
00:39:00,588 --> 00:39:04,258
in the morning meeting each other halfway,

538
00:39:05,301 --> 00:39:10,014
but coming out of one single room…

539
00:39:10,097 --> 00:39:11,557
[jazz music playing]

540
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:14,393
after a memorable night.

541
00:39:21,609 --> 00:39:29,116
Now that, I would dare say, is perfection.

542
00:39:32,953 --> 00:39:37,500
-Oh, you silly cow.
-The silly cow still has it.

543
00:39:38,250 --> 00:39:39,627
Or have you forgotten?

544
00:39:40,920 --> 00:39:43,672
But, as much as I would like to join you,

545
00:39:44,340 --> 00:39:46,801
I have some pressing engagements

546
00:39:46,884 --> 00:39:48,969
that I have to attend to this morning.

547
00:39:50,137 --> 00:39:52,390
My lady, I have to go.

548
00:40:02,024 --> 00:40:03,609
-Sir.
-Hi.

549
00:40:03,984 --> 00:40:06,737
Good mood? You look inspired.

550
00:40:07,363 --> 00:40:12,952
I'm in a very, very good mood.
And I am very inspired.

551
00:40:14,245 --> 00:40:18,124
Before this day is done, Colonel,

552
00:40:18,666 --> 00:40:23,045
I will show you that Julio Ardiente

553
00:40:23,671 --> 00:40:28,592
is still king of the province of Ardiente.

554
00:40:29,260 --> 00:40:30,219
[ominous music playing]

555
00:40:30,302 --> 00:40:32,012
That governor position?

556
00:40:32,721 --> 00:40:33,848
[scoffs]

557
00:40:33,931 --> 00:40:36,934
It's going to be crawling back to me,

558
00:40:37,726 --> 00:40:42,606
like a jilted lover
begging for a second chance,

559
00:40:42,690 --> 00:40:44,650
pleading to be loved.

560
00:40:46,485 --> 00:40:48,070
Watch and learn, Colonel.

561
00:40:48,904 --> 00:40:49,947
[scoffs]

562
00:40:54,243 --> 00:40:55,911
Goodbye, my love.

563
00:40:56,537 --> 00:40:57,580
Farewell.

564
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:00,749
[Julio laughs softly]

565
00:41:02,334 --> 00:41:03,335
[Julio] Ah…

566
00:41:08,632 --> 00:41:11,677
Sir, our men are with one of the witnesses

567
00:41:11,760 --> 00:41:13,137
of Camia's shooting.

568
00:41:13,804 --> 00:41:16,515
It's a good thing we have an early start.

569
00:41:16,974 --> 00:41:19,935
Too many people saw me shoot Camia.

570
00:41:21,187 --> 00:41:23,731
Typical Filipinos. So nosy. Oh.

571
00:41:25,065 --> 00:41:29,278
Good morning, Teacher Liza.

572
00:41:29,361 --> 00:41:32,072
Good morning. What do you want?

573
00:41:32,156 --> 00:41:34,325
What are you going to do to me?
Please don't kill me.

574
00:41:34,408 --> 00:41:35,284
[sobbing]

575
00:41:35,367 --> 00:41:38,454
Is that really how you think of me?

576
00:41:39,788 --> 00:41:41,874
Do I look like a murderer?

577
00:41:43,501 --> 00:41:46,170
I'm just here to talk.

578
00:41:49,423 --> 00:41:50,466
[sighs]

579
00:41:51,342 --> 00:41:55,888
Here's 50,000 pesos, Teacher Liza.

580
00:41:57,056 --> 00:42:02,853
All that I ask is for you
not to testify against me…

581
00:42:04,605 --> 00:42:08,943
in the case of Camia Cruz's shooting.

582
00:42:09,527 --> 00:42:10,277
Huh?

583
00:42:14,240 --> 00:42:15,533
Take it.

584
00:42:16,200 --> 00:42:19,662
An act of kindness
from one neighbor to another.

585
00:42:22,790 --> 00:42:25,084
By the way, before I forget.

586
00:42:25,876 --> 00:42:28,170
Um… The other reason
why I'm here is to ask you

587
00:42:28,254 --> 00:42:30,297
if you can help me find these people.

588
00:42:30,381 --> 00:42:35,427
[suspenseful music playing]

589
00:42:42,059 --> 00:42:45,187
Today is a very, very good day
because today,

590
00:42:45,563 --> 00:42:48,148
you will expose Lily Cruz as your enemy.

591
00:42:48,524 --> 00:42:50,859
And I already hired a private investigator

592
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:52,945
and all the surprises.

593
00:42:54,154 --> 00:42:55,072
Mama?

594
00:42:55,155 --> 00:42:56,991
Yeah. That's great. That's great.

595
00:42:57,074 --> 00:43:00,369
Mama, I still haven't spoken
to my friend, Jaguar.

596
00:43:01,370 --> 00:43:04,582
[Helena] Well, when you do talk
to him, that's when we'll know

597
00:43:04,665 --> 00:43:08,961
whether or not he was the one
who sabotaged my shipment.

598
00:43:09,044 --> 00:43:10,296
[suspenseful music playing]

599
00:43:13,799 --> 00:43:16,010
Hey! Who's there?!

600
00:43:17,636 --> 00:43:20,306
Look, someone hiding there.
Who on earth is that?

601
00:43:20,973 --> 00:43:23,225
Why don't you show your face?!
Get down from there.

602
00:43:25,352 --> 00:43:27,396
Sorry, I just took care
of something at the back.

603
00:43:27,688 --> 00:43:29,523
Mama, that's my husband Raul.

604
00:43:29,607 --> 00:43:31,400
Raul, come. Join us.

605
00:43:33,277 --> 00:43:34,445
How are you, Mama?

606
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:41,118
Humor me, how did a lazy-eyed
moose like you, of all people,

607
00:43:41,201 --> 00:43:43,704
end up marrying my one and only daughter?

608
00:43:43,787 --> 00:43:44,747
Mama.

609
00:43:44,830 --> 00:43:46,123
Well, what do you do?

610
00:43:46,582 --> 00:43:50,294
I have a… I run a small jewelry business.

611
00:43:51,211 --> 00:43:55,132
Emilia, I didn't know
you had a thing for peasants.

612
00:43:55,299 --> 00:43:56,342
Mama!

613
00:43:57,551 --> 00:43:58,886
It's not like that--

614
00:43:58,969 --> 00:44:01,639
I've heard enough. It's okay.

615
00:44:03,724 --> 00:44:05,726
Sit down. Join us.

616
00:44:18,238 --> 00:44:18,989
[Emilia] Eat.

617
00:44:21,450 --> 00:44:23,869
Mrs. Loring! Mister Pandoy!

618
00:44:25,037 --> 00:44:27,289
Mrs. Loring! Mister Pandoy!

619
00:44:29,541 --> 00:44:30,709
Mrs. Liza?

620
00:44:31,710 --> 00:44:33,712
Nanny! Uncle! It's Mrs. Liza!

621
00:44:34,254 --> 00:44:36,006
Hey, Liza.

622
00:44:36,590 --> 00:44:38,509
Good day to you.

623
00:44:38,592 --> 00:44:39,718
Oh, Liza!

624
00:44:39,802 --> 00:44:40,678
[Liza] Ah…

625
00:44:41,637 --> 00:44:42,596
Mrs. Loring.

626
00:44:44,098 --> 00:44:45,307
Mister Pandoy.

627
00:44:47,351 --> 00:44:49,019
Mrs. Liza, is there a problem?

628
00:44:50,145 --> 00:44:51,271
Diego…

629
00:44:53,315 --> 00:44:55,609
Julio Ardiente approached me earlier.

630
00:44:57,403 --> 00:44:59,405
[suspenseful music playing]

631
00:45:31,437 --> 00:45:33,856
Ms. Dang, Nikki,
please watch over the stove.

632
00:45:33,939 --> 00:45:35,107
-Yes, ma'am.
-Thank you.

633
00:45:39,069 --> 00:45:40,070
Lily.

634
00:45:44,283 --> 00:45:46,452
I feel like someone's watching us, Mom.

635
00:45:48,287 --> 00:45:51,415
Lily, don't you think
you're just being paranoid?

636
00:45:55,794 --> 00:45:56,962
I'm sorry, Mom.

637
00:45:58,046 --> 00:46:01,091
But as long as our enemies are alive,

638
00:46:01,175 --> 00:46:02,885
I'll never be at peace.

639
00:46:03,969 --> 00:46:05,137
And, that's why

640
00:46:05,721 --> 00:46:08,432
I'm going to meet up
with our anonymous informant.

641
00:46:09,558 --> 00:46:13,353
They might be able to help us
corner Red Dragon.

642
00:46:14,813 --> 00:46:19,401
Just keep your eyes open, okay?
This could be a trap.

643
00:46:20,277 --> 00:46:22,279
Don't just put your trust in them.

644
00:46:23,572 --> 00:46:26,283
I'm sorry, Mom,
but I'll still take that risk.

645
00:46:27,367 --> 00:46:31,038
And that's because I'm done playing games

646
00:46:31,121 --> 00:46:32,539
with Red Dragon.

647
00:46:32,623 --> 00:46:34,833
I've lost my patience.

648
00:46:42,508 --> 00:46:43,759
[Julio] This is for you.

649
00:46:44,343 --> 00:46:48,555
Just don't testify
that you saw me shoot Camia--

650
00:46:48,639 --> 00:46:50,265
[Diego] And what do we have here?!

651
00:46:51,475 --> 00:46:52,601
[Julio] Excuse me.

652
00:46:54,728 --> 00:46:56,230
You just can't accept defeat, can you?

653
00:46:56,313 --> 00:46:57,397
[Julio laughs]

654
00:46:58,524 --> 00:46:59,900
Of course!

655
00:47:00,526 --> 00:47:04,655
An Ardiente never accepts defeat or loses.

656
00:47:05,405 --> 00:47:09,993
An Ardiente will never
just let this thing sli--

657
00:47:10,077 --> 00:47:12,037
So, you're threatening and bribing

658
00:47:12,120 --> 00:47:14,831
Aunt Camia's witnesses against you,

659
00:47:15,666 --> 00:47:18,168
now that your 90-day suspension
is almost over!

660
00:47:19,294 --> 00:47:20,879
-Yes.
-I know what you're up to.

661
00:47:21,547 --> 00:47:24,132
You're cleaning up all the mess
that can prevent you

662
00:47:24,216 --> 00:47:25,592
from returning to power.

663
00:47:26,260 --> 00:47:28,929
But what makes you so sure
that you can ever return?!

664
00:47:30,013 --> 00:47:33,600
Diego, for an Ardiente like me,

665
00:47:34,226 --> 00:47:40,649
politics is like a very long plane ride.

666
00:47:42,192 --> 00:47:45,279
You'll be flying high for hours
and hours until the plane

667
00:47:46,363 --> 00:47:48,782
descends from the sky

668
00:47:50,867 --> 00:47:52,160
to land for refueling.

669
00:47:53,036 --> 00:47:58,375
After which,
it will take to the skies again

670
00:47:59,376 --> 00:48:01,461
for another long journey.

671
00:48:02,879 --> 00:48:04,715
At this point, I have refueled, Diego,

672
00:48:04,798 --> 00:48:09,136
so I won't stay on the ground any longer.

673
00:48:09,219 --> 00:48:10,345
I'm ready to soar once more.

674
00:48:10,429 --> 00:48:12,139
You're all talk.

675
00:48:14,891 --> 00:48:18,562
I'll make sure
that this is your last ride!

676
00:48:20,689 --> 00:48:22,274
[tense music playing]

677
00:48:24,192 --> 00:48:25,485
You know what?

678
00:48:26,528 --> 00:48:31,158
I will never be stopped
by a loser like you!

679
00:48:36,413 --> 00:48:37,331
Sir!

680
00:48:37,914 --> 00:48:40,083
Don't kid yourself.

681
00:48:40,167 --> 00:48:42,711
You only won because you cheated!

682
00:48:44,796 --> 00:48:46,465
You bastard!

683
00:48:47,674 --> 00:48:48,467
Sir.

684
00:48:49,885 --> 00:48:51,470
-Sir… Sir?
-[Julio grunts]

685
00:48:53,513 --> 00:48:54,723
Remember, Julio.

686
00:48:56,683 --> 00:48:59,061
As long as I'm alive,

687
00:48:59,144 --> 00:49:02,022
you'll never be
the governor of this province.

688
00:49:03,815 --> 00:49:05,192
Remember that!

689
00:49:07,944 --> 00:49:10,364
[tense music playing]

690
00:49:14,159 --> 00:49:16,036
<i>This is a clone of Mercedes' phone.</i>

691
00:49:16,119 --> 00:49:17,704
[Jepoy] <i>You can keep track</i>
<i>of all her calls</i>

692
00:49:17,788 --> 00:49:19,498
<i>and text messages from here.</i>

693
00:49:19,581 --> 00:49:20,415
[Camia] <i>It's confirmed.</i>

694
00:49:20,499 --> 00:49:23,085
<i>That's another piece of evidence</i>
<i>that will prove</i>

695
00:49:23,168 --> 00:49:25,671
<i>that Helena Montoya is Red Dragon.</i>

696
00:49:25,754 --> 00:49:27,798
[Diego] <i>I've waited so long</i>
<i>to give you this.</i>

697
00:49:29,049 --> 00:49:30,384
<i>I love you so much.</i>

698
00:49:30,884 --> 00:49:32,719
[Anna] <i>Why are you so happy?</i>

699
00:49:32,803 --> 00:49:34,596
[Arnaldo] <i>I think I saw an angel.</i>

700
00:49:34,680 --> 00:49:35,889
<i>Is she my brother's girlfriend?</i>

701
00:49:35,972 --> 00:49:37,474
[Jepoy] <i>What if the old Arnaldo</i>
<i>comes back?</i>

702
00:49:37,557 --> 00:49:39,810
<i>The cruel Arnaldo. Are we still</i>
<i>going to protect him?</i>

703
00:49:39,893 --> 00:49:41,728
[Anna] <i>If that does happen, Jepoy,</i>

704
00:49:41,812 --> 00:49:43,563
<i>are you going to kill him?</i>

705
00:49:43,647 --> 00:49:45,357
<i>Yes. Without a doubt.</i>

706
00:49:46,066 --> 00:49:47,317
<i>Jepoy!</i>

707
00:49:47,401 --> 00:49:49,778
[theme music playing]
